# @zmkfirmware/zmk-studio-ts-client ships a devDependency-only postinstall
# (`run-script-os`) that fails on every platform for consumers — the package
# is not installed, so the script errors before it can even check whether
# there's anything to build (there isn't; the package ships prebuilt output
# under lib/). Same issue and same fix as web/.npmrc.
#
# This repo also depends on esbuild / @swc/core / protobufjs, which each ship
# their own postinstall script, but none of them are load-bearing here:
#   - esbuild's install.js and @swc/core's postinstall.js only *verify* the
#     platform-specific native binary that npm already installed via
#     optionalDependencies; both packages require that binary directly at
#     runtime regardless of whether the postinstall verification ran.
#   - protobufjs's postinstall only prints a version-mismatch lint warning.
#
# Setting ignore-scripts here means a plain `npm install` (no extra flags)
# works everywhere.
ignore-scripts=true
